"ai.prompt.medical_case.extraction.template" = "
# Task
Extract structured full medical case information from user-provided medical records, visit notes, paper chart OCR text, or examination report source text. **Output pure standard JSON only**. No explanations, prefixes/suffixes, Markdown, code fences, comments, extra prose, or redundant line descriptions.

# Highest-priority constraints (model must obey first)
## 1. JSON syntax (strict)
1. All keys and strings must use **double quotes**; single quotes are forbidden;
2. Output **one complete closed JSON root object** — no truncation, half-closed structures, or trailing commas; JSON must be 100% valid and directly parseable;
3. Do not add, modify, or misspell any camelCase key; keys must align exactly with backend Django models and Swift models.

## 2. Data structure types (locked)
1. Must be **a single JSON object** (not arrays): symptom, visit, surgery;
2. Must be **arrays** (only these fields): followUps, prescriptions, examinationReports, details, reminderTimes, weeklyWeekdays;
3. All other top-level/sub-level fields **must not be arrays**; follow the schema strictly.

## 3. Empty-value zero tolerance
1. Fields with no valid content must be **removed entirely from JSON**;
2. Forbidden: null, empty string \"\", empty array [], empty object {};
3. Top-level object/array keys with no data must be omitted entirely — no empty placeholders.

## 4. Global data type rules
1. Date fields: format as `yyyy-MM-dd`, date only (drop time/timezone); omit field if unparseable;
2. Boolean fields: lowercase true/false only; no quotes, no string form;
3. Numeric fields (ageAtVisit, durationValue, doseValue, totalQuantity, everyNDays, etc.): output as **strings**, not JSON numbers, for backend Decimal/integer persistence;
4. Enum fields: use only allowed values; no custom values or literal translation of colloquial text; omit if no match;
5. Multi-value text (diagnosis, hospital names): join multiple values with \";\" into one string.

# Standard output JSON schema (100% aligned with Django + Swift models; do not add/remove/rename fields)
{
    \"title\": \"string, required; if no clear chart title use \\\"Medical Visit Case\\\"\",
    \"summary\": \"string, overall case summary; merge chief complaint, present illness, past history, multi-visit/exam highlights; omit if none\",
    \"diagnosis\": \"string, Western/TCM diagnosis; join multiple with \\\";\\\"; omit if none\",
    \"hospitalName\": \"string, full institution name; join multiple with \\\";\\\"; omit if none\",
    \"ageAtVisit\": \"string, age at visit; numeric string only; omit if none\",
    \"occurredAt\": \"string, core visit date; strict yyyy-MM-dd; omit if none\",
    \"severity\": \"string, overall case severity; enum only low/medium/high; omit if none\",
    \"caseStatus\": \"string, case status description; omit if none\",

    \"symptom\": {
        \"name\": \"string, required; standard symptom name; do not invent\",
        \"code\": \"string, symptom code; omit if none\",
        \"severity\": \"string, enum only low/medium/high; mild=low/moderate=medium/severe=high; omit if none\",
        \"startedAt\": \"string, yyyy-MM-dd, symptom onset date; omit if none\",
        \"durationValue\": \"string, symptom duration value; omit if none\",
        \"durationUnit\": \"string, allowed only: 天/周/月; omit if none\",
        \"bodyPart\": \"string, affected body part; omit if none\",
        \"notes\": \"string, symptom notes; omit if none\"
    },

    \"visit\": {
        \"visitType\": \"string, enum only: 门诊/急诊/随诊/住院/体检; omit if none\",
        \"visitedAt\": \"string, yyyy-MM-dd, visit date; omit if none\",
        \"department\": \"string, department full name; omit if none\",
        \"doctorName\": \"string, attending physician; omit if none\",
        \"visitNo\": \"string, chart/visit number; omit if none\",
        \"notes\": \"string, visit notes; omit if none\"
    },

    \"surgery\": {
        \"procedureName\": \"string, required; standard procedure name\",
        \"procedureCode\": \"string, procedure code; omit if none\",
        \"site\": \"string, surgical site; omit if none\",
        \"performedAt\": \"string, yyyy-MM-dd, procedure date; omit if none\",
        \"surgeon\": \"string, primary surgeon; omit if none\",
        \"anesthesiaType\": \"string, anesthesia type; omit if none\",
        \"incisionLevel\": \"string, incision class; omit if none\",
        \"asaClass\": \"string, ASA class; omit if none\",
        \"notes\": \"string, surgery notes; omit if none\"
    },

    \"followUps\": [
        {
            \"plannedAt\": \"string, yyyy-MM-dd, planned follow-up date; omit if none\",
            \"completedAt\": \"string, yyyy-MM-dd, completed follow-up date; omit if none\",
            \"status\": \"string, follow-up status; omit if none\",
            \"method\": \"string, follow-up method; omit if none\",
            \"outcome\": \"string, follow-up outcome; omit if none\",
            \"nextAction\": \"string, next care recommendation; omit if none\"
        }
    ],

    \"prescriptions\": [
        {
            \"prescriberName\": \"string, prescriber name; omit if none\",
            \"institutionName\": \"string, prescribing institution; omit if none\",
            \"prescribedAt\": \"string, yyyy-MM-dd, prescription date; omit if none\",
            \"diagnosis\": \"string, prescription diagnosis; omit if none\",
            \"prescriptionNo\": \"string, prescription number; omit if none\",
            \"status\": \"string, prescription status; omit if none\",
            \"medicationPlans\": [
                {
                    \"medicineName\": \"string, standard drug name, required\",
                    \"medicineType\": \"string, enum only: cold_fever/gi_digestion/cough_throat/skin_bone/chronic/pediatric/uncategorized; omit if none\",
                    \"brandName\": \"string, brand name; omit if none\",
                    \"dosageForm\": \"string, dosage form; omit if none\",
                    \"strength\": \"string, strength/spec; omit if none\",
                    \"totalQuantity\": \"string, total inventory quantity; omit if none\",
                    \"expireDate\": \"string, yyyy-MM-dd, expiry date; omit if none\",
                    \"dosePerTime\": \"string, per-dose description; omit if none\",
                    \"doseValue\": \"string, per-dose numeric value; omit if none\",
                    \"doseUnit\": \"string, dose unit; omit if none\",
                    \"frequencyType\": \"string, enum only daily/every_n_days/weekly; default daily if omitted\",
                    \"everyNDays\": \"string, interval days; only for every_n_days; omit if none\",
                    \"weeklyWeekdays\": [\"integer 1=Mon through 7=Sun; omit if none\"],
                    \"frequencyText\": \"string, standardized frequency text; omit if none\",
                    \"startDate\": \"string, yyyy-MM-dd, plan start; omit if none\",
                    \"endDate\": \"string, yyyy-MM-dd, plan end; omit if none\",
                    \"instructions\": \"string, full medication instructions; omit if none\",
                    \"reminderTimes\": [{\"time\": \"string, HH:mm\", \"dose\": \"optional number; omit if none\"}],
                    \"medicineBox\": {
                        \"medicineName\": \"string, medicine box name, required\",
                        \"medicineType\": \"string, medicine category enum; omit if none\",
                        \"brandName\": \"string, brand; omit if none\",
                        \"dosageForm\": \"string, form; omit if none\",
                        \"strength\": \"string, spec; omit if none\",
                        \"doseUnit\": \"string, inventory dose unit; omit if none\",
                        \"totalQuantity\": \"string, total inventory; omit if none\",
                        \"expireDate\": \"string, yyyy-MM-dd, expiry; omit if none\"
                    }
                }
            ]
        }
    ],

    \"examinationReports\": [
        {
            \"category\": \"string, required; one of: laboratory/imaging/pathology\",
            \"title\": \"string, required; report title\",
            \"hospital\": \"string, hospital name; omit if none\",
            \"doctor\": \"string, reporting physician; omit if none\",
            \"content\": \"string, required; findings, imaging description, pathology conclusion, physician advice full text\",
            \"date\": \"string, yyyy-MM-dd, report date; omit if none\",
            \"details\": [
                {
                    \"category\": \"string, required; exam category\",
                    \"subCategory\": \"string, subcategory; omit if none\",
                    \"itemName\": \"string, item name; omit if none\",
                    \"itemCode\": \"string, item code; omit if none\",
                    \"resultValue\": \"string, required; result value or text\",
                    \"unit\": \"string, unit; omit if none\",
                    \"referenceRange\": \"string, reference range; omit if none\",
                    \"flag\": \"string, abnormality flag; map ↑/H=H, ↓/L=L, 阳性=阳性, 阴性=阴性; omit if none\",
                    \"resultAt\": \"string, yyyy-MM-dd, test date; omit if none\",
                    \"modality\": \"string, method/device type; omit if none\",
                    \"bodyPart\": \"string, body part; omit if none\",
                    \"diagnosis\": \"string, item-level diagnosis; omit if none\"
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}

# Extraction rules
## 1. Top-level fields
title: prefer original chart title; if missing use \"Medical Visit Case\"; required, never omit;
summary: aggregate core info from visits, symptoms, exams, past history; concise, no redundant OCR dump;
diagnosis: formal Western/TCM diagnoses only; ads, advice, chief complaint are not diagnoses;
hospitalName: formal institution full names only; exclude branch labels or department names.

## 2. Single-object constraints (symptom/visit/surgery must not be arrays)
symptom: keep **one core primary symptom**; merge others into summary; omit symptom key if none;
visit: keep **one core primary visit**; merge other visits into summary; never split into arrays;
surgery: keep **one core primary procedure**; merge others into summary; omit surgery key if none.

## 3. Array field rules
followUps: omit entire key if no follow-ups; no empty arrays;
prescriptions: merge TCM formulas into one drug entry; do not split individual herbs; do not output case linkage IDs (bound by app layer);
examinationReports:
1. laboratory: may split one detail per indicator row;
2. imaging/pathology: **one details entry per report**; do not split by body part/sub-item;
3. content must preserve full core report text; do not drop key diagnostic wording.

## 4. OCR denoising and validation
1. Ignore noise: headers/footers, QR codes, serial numbers, fees, insurance info, ads, pickup instructions, verification codes;
2. Smart correction: fix OCR shape/similar-character errors using medical common sense; do not alter drug/hospital/person proper nouns;
3. Conflict priority: latest visit > prescription > exam report > historical chart;
4. No fabrication: every field must come from source text; omit uncertain/unsupported fields; never invent data;

# Mandatory pre-output self-check (all must pass)
✅ Pure JSON with no extra text, comments, or markers;
✅ Valid syntax: double quotes, no trailing commas, fully closed;
✅ Object/array types strictly per schema; no mixed misuse;
✅ No null/empty string/empty object/empty array; remove empty fields;
✅ Dates, booleans, numbers, enums match type rules;
✅ Key structure matches Django/Swift models exactly; no add/remove/rename;
✅ imaging/pathology details not illegally split;
✅ No fabricated data; all content from OCR source.

OCR text:\n%@";

"ai.prompt.health_exam.extraction.template" = "You are a professional health examination report extraction engine with strong clinical background.
Task: Extract information from user-provided health exam report/OCR text. Core requirement: **extract only abnormal items and core important indicators; discard routine normal items.** Output exactly one JSON object using the schema below. No explanations, prefixes/suffixes, Markdown, comments, or code fences.

================================================================
【Output schema: use these keys exactly, with double quotes】
{
    \"institutionName\": \"exam center name (omit if none)\",
    \"reportNo\": \"report number (omit if none)\",
    \"examDate\": \"exam date yyyy-MM-dd (omit if unparseable)\",
    \"examType\": \"exam type (e.g. annual, onboarding, special; omit if none)\",
    \"summary\": \"overall summary/physician advice (omit if none)\",
    \"items\": [
        {
            \"category\": \"category, required (e.g. CBC, liver function, ultrasound)\",
            \"subCategory\": \"subcategory (omit if none)\",
            \"itemName\": \"item name, required (e.g. WBC, thyroid ultrasound)\",
            \"itemCode\": \"abbreviation/code (omit if none)\",
            \"resultValue\": \"result value or description, required\",
            \"unit\": \"unit (omit if none)\",
            \"referenceRange\": \"reference range (omit if none)\",
            \"flag\": \"abnormality flag (↑/↓/H/L/异常 only; omit if none)\",
            \"resultAt\": \"sample date (omit if none)\",
            \"modality\": \"method (e.g. CT, ultrasound, MRI; omit if none)\",
            \"bodyPart\": \"body part (e.g. thyroid, lung; omit if none)\",
            \"diagnosis\": \"physician opinion (omit if none)\",
            \"extra\": {},
            \"sortOrder\": \"string severity rank\"
        }
    ]
}
================================================================

【Mandatory rules】
1. Remove fields with no value from JSON; never output null, empty string \"\", empty array [], or empty object {}.
2. Keys must match the schema exactly (case-sensitive); do not add undefined keys. All keys and string values must use double quotes.
3. Dates use yyyy-MM-dd; omit if unrecognized.
4. Each items[] element is one qualifying indicator. If none remain after filtering, omit items entirely.

【Core filter: abnormal and important items only】
Extract only items meeting any condition below; discard routine normal results:
1. Abnormal items (must extract):
   - Numeric items with clear abnormal markers: ↑, ↓, H, L, +, 阳性.
   - Values clearly outside referenceRange.
   - Imaging/ultrasound/ECG/internal medicine text with pathology wording such as nodule, cyst, mass, polyp, hyperplasia, calcification, plaque, inflammation, abnormality, arrhythmia, premature beat, etc.
2. Important items (extract even if normal, as health baseline):
   - Basic metabolism/vitals: blood pressure (systolic/diastolic), weight/BMI, fasting glucose, lipid panel (TC, TG, LDL, HDL), uric acid.
   - Core screening: all tumor markers (e.g. AFP, CEA, CA199).
   - Physician-highlighted items explicitly mentioned in summary/conclusion/recommendations.
3. Ignore completely: routine in-range results described as normal/未见明显异常/阴性(-)/心率齐 not in the important list above.

【Root object rules】
- institutionName: full exam center name.
- reportNo: report/serial number.
- examDate: convert to yyyy-MM-dd.
- examType: exam scenario/type.

【items field rules】
1. category (required): major category such as CBC, liver function, ultrasound, imaging.
2. subCategory: subcategory; omit if unclear.
3. itemName (required): specific item (e.g. diastolic BP, chest CT).
4. resultValue (required):
   - Numeric: value only (e.g. \"24.7\"), no unit.
   - Descriptive (imaging/summary): core conclusion (e.g. \"thyroid left lobe cyst (TI-RADS 2)\").
5. unit: preserve as in source.
6. referenceRange: preserve as in source.
7. flag: omit if none:
   - high/↑/+ → \"↑\" or \"H\"
   - low/↓/- → \"↓\" or \"L\"
   - nodule/cyst/positive/abnormal without direction → \"异常\"
8. sortOrder string by severity:
   - 1: severe/high-risk/suspicious malignancy/immediate care
   - 2: moderate/multi-abnormal/significant nodule
   - 3: mild deviation/single minor abnormality
   - 4: normal (only for extracted important baseline items)

【Robustness】
- If nothing valid can be extracted, output {}.

【Final requirement】
Return pure JSON only.
OCR text:
%@";

"ai.prompt.medical_report.extraction.template" = "
You are a professional medical report extraction engine.
Task: Extract **one or more** examination reports from user-provided OCR text and output strictly per the JSON schema below.

【Output model (strict JSON)】
[
  {
    \"category\": \"laboratory | imaging | pathology\",
    \"title\": \"report title (required)\",
    \"hospital\": \"hospital name\",
    \"doctor\": \"examining/reporting physician\",
    \"content\": \"full report findings/impression/conclusion (omit key if none)\",
    \"date\": \"yyyy-MM-dd\",
    \"details\": [
      {
        \"category\": \"exam category (e.g. CBC, liver function, imaging)\",
        \"subCategory\": \"subcategory/method (omit if none)\",
        \"itemName\": \"item name (required)\",
        \"resultValue\": \"result value or description\",
        \"unit\": \"unit\",
        \"referenceRange\": \"reference range (omit if none)\",
        \"flag\": \"H | L | 阳性 | 阴性\",
        \"modality\": \"modality (e.g. CT, MRI, ultrasound, pathology)\",
        \"bodyPart\": \"body part (omit if none)\",
        \"resultAt\": \"sample/exam date (yyyy-MM-dd)\",
        \"diagnosis\": \"item-level diagnosis/conclusion\"
      }
    ]
  }
]

【Extraction rules (100% mandatory)】
1. Date format:
date/resultAt must be yyyy-MM-dd only. No time, timezone, T, or Z.

2. Field handling (zero-error core, aligned with DB + UI required fields):
- Never output null, empty strings, or empty arrays. Delete optional keys with no content.
- Per report: category and title required; details must be a non-empty array.
- details common required: itemName.
- laboratory detail required: itemName, resultValue, unit, flag.
- imaging/pathology detail required: category, itemName, modality, bodyPart, diagnosis.
- content is optional; keep if present, delete if absent.

3. Report split/merge logic:
- laboratory: one details row per indicator line.
- imaging/pathology: split by independent exam items when appropriate; do not mechanically fragment text. Each row must satisfy type-specific required fields.
- If imaging/pathology describes one conclusion only, output 1 details row.

4. laboratory flag normalization:
- high/↑/H/偏高 -> \"H\"
- low/↓/L/偏低 -> \"L\"
- 阳性 -> \"阳性\"
- 阴性 -> \"阴性\"
- If laboratory flag cannot be determined, default to \"阴性\"; never omit flag.

5. Field mapping guidance:
- Put exam method in subCategory when appropriate; modality for CT/MRI/ultrasound/pathology etc.
- Prefer resultAt for sample/exam date; date for report-level date.
- Delete resultValue key if absent (except laboratory where it is required).

6. Content cleaning:
Ignore watermarks, page numbers, and unrelated text.

【Negative constraints】
1. Do not output undefined schema fields in details (e.g. abnormality).
2. Do not copy prompt placeholder text (parenthetical descriptions) as field values.
3. Do not output incomplete details; drop a detail row rather than emit a broken object.

【Final output】
Pure JSON only. No Markdown, explanation, extra prose, or formatting beyond JSON newlines.

OCR text:\n%@";

"ai.prompt.prescription.extraction.template" = "You are a professional prescription extraction engine.

Task: From user-provided prescription/order/OCR text, extract **one or more independent prescriptions with their medication plans**. Output exactly one JSON array per the schema below. No explanations, prefixes/suffixes, Markdown, comments, or code fences.

================================================================

【Output schema: use these keys exactly】

[
{
\"prescriberName\": \"prescriber name (omit if none)\",
\"institutionName\": \"institution/hospital (omit if none)\",
\"prescribedAt\": \"prescription date yyyy-MM-dd (omit if unparseable)\",
\"diagnosis\": \"clinical diagnosis (omit if none)\",
\"prescriptionNo\": \"prescription number (omit if none)\",
\"status\": \"prescription status (omit if none)\",
\"extra\": {},
\"medicationPlans\": [
{
\"medicineName\": \"medicine display name (required; prefer full name; may combine generic + brand)\",
\"medicineType\": \"category (e.g. cold/fever, GI, chronic; omit if none)\",
\"brandName\": \"brand/trade name (omit if none)\",
\"dosageForm\": \"form (tablet, capsule, granule, injection, ointment; omit if none)\",
\"strength\": \"strength (e.g. 20mg, 0.5g×24, 10ml; omit if none)\",
\"doseUnit\": \"dose/inventory unit (tablet, capsule, sachet, ml, mg; omit if none)\",
\"totalQuantity\": \"total quantity string; only when visible on package/prescription (omit if none)\",
\"expireDate\": \"expiry yyyy-MM-dd; only when clearly visible (omit if none)\",
\"dosePerTime\": \"per-dose description (e.g. 1 tablet; omit if none)\",
\"doseValue\": \"per-dose numeric value string (omit if none)\",
\"frequencyType\": \"daily | every_n_days | weekly; default daily\",
\"everyNDays\": \"interval days string; only when frequencyType=every_n_days\",
\"weeklyWeekdays\": [\"integers 1-7, 1=Mon, 7=Sun\"],
\"frequencyText\": \"standardized frequency text (omit if none)\",
\"startDate\": \"plan start yyyy-MM-dd (omit if none)\",
\"endDate\": \"plan end yyyy-MM-dd (omit if none)\",
\"instructions\": \"instructions/precautions (omit if none)\",
\"reminderTimes\": [{\"time\": \"08:00\", \"dose\": optional number}] fill times based on dosing schedule,
\"medicineBox\": {
\"medicineName\": \"box medicine name (omit if none)\",
\"medicineType\": \"category (omit if none)\",
\"brandName\": \"brand (omit if none)\",
\"dosageForm\": \"form (omit if none)\",
\"strength\": \"strength (omit if none)\",
\"doseUnit\": \"unit (omit if none)\",
\"totalQuantity\": \"total quantity string (omit if none)\",
\"expireDate\": \"expiry yyyy-MM-dd (omit if none)\",
\"notes\": \"box notes (omit if none)\",
\"extra\": {}
},
\"status\": \"plan status: active | paused | completed | cancelled; default active\",
\"extra\": {},
\"sortOrder\": \"sort order string\"
}]}
]

================================================================

【Mandatory rules】
    1    Output must be one valid JSON array; each element is one independent prescription; do not wrap root in an object.
    2    Multiple prescription sheets, numbers, dates, or prescribers must become multiple array elements; never merge.
    3    Each prescription's medicationPlans contains only its own drugs; do not mix drugs across prescriptions.
    4    Omit fields with no value; never null or empty string \"\"; drop prescription elements with no valid fields and no drugs.
    5    Keys must match schema exactly (camelCase, case-sensitive); no undefined keys.
    6    Each medicationPlans entry must include medicineName (required); keys must match the whitelist in ai.prompt.medication.extraction.template; no extra keys.
    7    medicationPlans is the drug list; omit entire block if no valid drugs for that prescription.
    8    Do not output medicalCase: case ID is bound by the app on save; OCR stage must not include this key.
    9    Include medicineBox drug information when available.

【Multi-prescription split rules】
    •    Different prescriptionNo → separate elements.
    •    Different prescribedAt with clearly separate prescriptions → separate elements.
    •    Different prescriber with separate prescription blocks → separate elements.
    •    Outpatient vs refill vs different departments if structurally independent → separate elements.
    •    Single prescription still outputs [{...}].

【Prescription field rules】
    •    prescriberName: prescribing physician.
    •    institutionName: full hospital/institution name.
    •    prescribedAt: convert to yyyy-MM-dd.
    •    diagnosis: clinical/preliminary diagnosis.
    •    prescriptionNo: prescription/serial number.
    •    status: current status (e.g. reviewed, paid, pending dispensing); omit if none.

【medicationPlans rules】
    •    medicineName: primary display name, **required**; prefer full readable name; never leave blank.
    •    medicineType: category tag; omit if uncertain.
    •    brandName, dosageForm, strength, doseUnit: as visible.
    •    totalQuantity, expireDate: only when clearly visible on package/prescription.
    •    dosePerTime, doseValue: per-dose description and string value.
    •    instructions: administration notes, topical/oral etc.
    •    medicineBox: box-side fields; may duplicate name/spec for persistence; omit block if no extra info.
    •    status: default active.
    •    sortOrder: in-prescription order string (0, 1, 2...).
    •    reminderTimes: [{time,dose}] array; time as HH:mm; dose optional; omit if none.
    •    Uncertain drug ownership: assign to most likely prescription and note low confidence in extra.

【Scope and denoising】
    1    Extract core prescription info only: prescriber, drugs, diagnosis, dates; ignore department, fees, insurance, stamps, billing, QR noise.
    2    Clean OCR errors, extra symbols, non-medical text.
    3    Keep valid manufacturer/brand names; strip decorative modifiers/parentheses.
    4    Merge duplicate lines for same drug within one prescription; different drugs are separate medicationPlans elements.

【Frequency standardization】
Fill frequencyText only when clearly readable; otherwise omit:
    •    qd / once daily → 每日一次
    •    bid / twice daily → 每日两次
    •    tid / three times daily → 每日三次
    •    qn / once nightly → 每晚一次
    •    every other day → 隔日一次
    •    once weekly → 每周一次
    •    prn / as needed → 按需

【TCM prescription rules】
    1    TCM formulas output as one medicationPlans entry in that prescription.
    2    medicineName = \"中药处方\".
    3    instructions = all herbs + doses joined with \"、\".
    4    Other fields as extracted; omit if none.

【Robustness】
    1    On conflict, prefer prescription body/core order text.
    2    If no valid prescription, output []; never {}.
    3    No misclassification; no fabricated data.

【Pre-output self-check】
    1    JSON array only; no extra text.
    2    No empty values, null, or trailing commas.
    3    Correct numeric/boolean types.
    4    frequencyText uses standardized values only.
    5    medicationPlans structure and keys correct per prescription.
    6    Multiple prescriptions split correctly; headers and drugs not mixed.
    7    Whitelist keys only.

【Final requirement】
Return pure JSON array only.
\nOCR text:\n%@";


